    "summary": "High‑energy set with stellar China>Rider and deep The Other One jam",
    "blurb": "The Brooklyn show delivers a ripping China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue and a powerful The Other One sequence. Jerry’s steel‑guitar work shines, and the band rides a high‑intensity groove throughout. Audio is muddy, but the performance quality makes it worth a listen.",
    "review": "On November 11, 1970 at Brooklyn’s 46th Street Rock Palace the Dead were in top form, feeding off an electric audience that kept the energy humming from start to finish. Highlights include a blistering China Cat Sunflower into I Know You Rider transition, a haunting Cryptical Envelopment → The Other One suite that builds into one of the night’s most adventurous jams, and a bright Sugar Magnolia that caps a set packed with classic Americana. Jerry Garcia’s steel‑guitar work—still fresh from his NRPS side project—and his onstage camaraderie with the crowd were repeatedly praised, while Pigpen’s keyboard textures sit solidly under the groove. The tape quality is far from pristine; both audience recordings are riddled with dropouts and a muddy low end, but the Cotsman source (gd70-11-11.aud.cotsman.17081.sbeok.shnf) captures the band’s dynamics better than any alternative, making it the preferred listen for anyone wanting to experience this high‑octane night.",
